@title a short name for somebody you name often

A nickname is your own abbreviation for another person's name.
Nobody else sees it: it is there so you type less.

  nickname <nickname> <name>   creates it, or changes one you had.
  nickname <nickname>          says what name it stands for.
  nickname                     lists every one you have.
  unnickname <nickname>        deletes it.

Wherever somebody's name is expected, the nickname works just as
well: after "nickname g Guard", "tell g hello" talks to the guard.
